  "_recorded": {
    "what": "the POST /v1.4x/containers/create body a stock docker CLI sends for `docker run --rm alpine true`",
    "client": "docker 29.4.0-ce (Docker CLI, linux/amd64)",
    "captured": "2026-08-22, by pointing DOCKER_HOST at a recording unix socket that logged the request body verbatim",
    "why": "issue #338. The allowlist in handleCreate is evaluated on NON-EMPTY values, and this file is the measurement that says which values are non-empty in practice. A hand-written list of field names is prose that drifts; this is what a real client really sent.",
    "refresh": "re-record it the same way against a newer client rather than hand-editing it. A key that changes emptiness must fail TestTheCreateAllowlistAdmitsWhatDockerActuallySends, not a user's `docker run`."
